Adds optional LLVM targets to the Bazel overlay.

An optional target's libraries (<T>Info, <T>UtilsAndDesc, <T>CodeGen, ...)
are declared, but the target stays out of the AllTargets* aggregates, the
LLVM shared library's roots, Targets.def and the LLVM_HAS_<T>_TARGET defines,
so only targets that depend on its libraries explicitly link them. The
per-target declaration loop reads llvm_all_target_lib_list; every other
reader keeps llvm_target_lib_list, which now lists builtin targets only. For
SPIRV, SPIRVAPI.cpp is left out because it needs the initializer
declarations that only Targets.def provides; its SPIRVTranslate* wrappers
have no other caller.

On an LLVM bump: refresh the hunks if they stop applying; if upstream adds
another per-target declaration loop, point it at llvm_all_target_lib_list
(other readers stay builtin-only); if SPIRVAPI.cpp gains callers, revisit the
exclusion. Drop this patch once upstream supports optional targets, or once
no target is optional.

diff --git a/utils/bazel/configure.bzl b/utils/bazel/configure.bzl
index f3bd939..1204efa 100644
--- a/utils/bazel/configure.bzl
+++ b/utils/bazel/configure.bzl
@@ -190,11 +190,15 @@ def _llvm_configure_impl(repository_ctx):
         executable = False,
     )
 
-    # Create a starlark file with the requested LLVM targets.
+    # Create a starlark file with the requested LLVM targets. Optional targets
+    # get their libraries but no place in the default aggregates, the LLVM
+    # shared library or the .def files; only explicit dependents link them.
     llvm_targets = repository_ctx.attr.targets
+    llvm_optional_targets = repository_ctx.attr.optional_targets
     repository_ctx.file(
         "llvm/targets.bzl",
-        content = "llvm_targets = " + str(llvm_targets),
+        content = "llvm_targets = " + str(llvm_targets) + "\n" +
+                  "llvm_optional_targets = " + str(llvm_optional_targets) + "\n",
         executable = False,
     )
 
@@ -214,5 +218,6 @@ llvm_configure = repository_rule(
     implementation = _llvm_configure_impl,
     attrs = {
         "targets": attr.string_list(default = DEFAULT_TARGETS),
+        "optional_targets": attr.string_list(default = []),
     },
 )
